<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maasai people</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Maasai are a Nilotic people of southern Kenya and northern Tanzania who speak Maa and traditionally live by herding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a>, organised in age sets of warriors and elders. In the 19th century they dominated much of the grazing land of the Rift Valley. Under British agreements of 1904 and 1911 they lost most of their best pastures in the central Kenya highlands to European settlers and were moved to southern reserves.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/maasai-people.jpg" alt="Maasai people" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Maasai_tribe.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
